{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-r9px-m959-cxf4","cve_id":"CVE-2025-21614","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-r9px-m959-cxf4","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-r9px-m959-cxf4","summary":"go-git clients vulnerable to DoS via maliciously crafted Git server replies","description":"### Impact\nA denial of service (DoS) vulnerability was discovered in go-git versions prior to `v5.13`. This vulnerability allows an attacker to perform denial of service attacks by providing specially crafted responses from a Git server which triggers resource exhaustion in `go-git` clients. \n\nThis is a `go-git` implementation issue and does not affect the upstream `git` cli.\n\n### Patches\nUsers running versions of `go-git` from `v4` and above are recommended to upgrade to `v5.13` in order to mitigate this vulnerability.\n\n### Workarounds\nIn cases where a bump to the latest version of `go-git` is not possible, we recommend limiting its use to only trust-worthy Git servers.\n\n## Credit\nThanks to Ionut Lalu for responsibly disclosing this vulnerability to us.","type":"reviewed","severity":"high","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/go-git/go-git/security-advisories/GHSA-r9px-m959-cxf4","source_code_location":"https://github.com/go-git/go-git","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-r9px-m959-cxf4","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2025-21614","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/go-git/go-git/security/advisories/GHSA-r9px-m959-cxf4","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-21614","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-r9px-m959-cxf4"],"published_at":"2025-01-06T16:20:28Z","updated_at":"2025-08-27T14:24:38Z","github_reviewed_at":"2025-01-06T16:20:28Z","nvd_published_at":"2025-01-06T17:15:47Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"go","name":"gopkg.in/src-d/go-git.v4"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 4.0.0, <= 4.13.1","first_patched_version":null,"vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"go","name":"github.com/go-git/go-git/v5"},"